{"qid":"Q685","names":["Solomon Islands"],"title":"Solomon Islands","endonym":{"native":"Solomon Islands","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The Solomon Islands is a Melanesian archipelago state in the southwestern Pacific comprising some 990 islands, which gained independence from Britain on 7 July 1978. The country experienced a severe period of ethnic conflict known as 'The Tensions' (1998–2003) between Guadalcanal and Malaita militias, resolved by the Regional Assistance Mission to Solomon Islands (RAMSI) led by Australia. Economically dependent on logging, fishing, and subsistence agriculture, the Solomon Islands has in recent years shifted diplomatic relations toward the People's Republic of China, signing a security agreement in 2022.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. National maritime boundaries are formally defined; the archipelago's land extent is geographically well-established.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Solomon Islands","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomon_Islands"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Regional Assistance Mission to Solomon Islands","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regional_Assistance_Mission_to_Solomon_Islands"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Solomon Islands–China relations","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomon_Islands%E2%80%93China_relations"},{"label":"Wikipedia: The Tensions (Solomon Islands)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Tensions"}],"britannica":"place/Solomon-Islands","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Solomon Islands","rulers":[{"qid":"Q425785","name":"Peter Kenilorea","start":1978,"end":1981,"image":"Peter Kenilorea (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.